    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37659" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-ĭcĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-jăcĭo</span></b>  or
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praejĭcĭo</span></b> , Fest. s. v.
		pone, p. 249 Müll.), jēci, jactum, 3,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to cast</i> or <i>throw up in
			front</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 8,
					17</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to cast up</i>, <i>object</i>, <i>utter
			reproachfully</i>: multis in contumeliam Graecorum praejactis
			probris, Dictys Cret. B. Troj. 2, 24.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
